      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2016 Elsevier Masson SAS. Tous droits réservés.",
        "AbstractText": "Since 1997, the World Health Organisation considered obesity, defined as an excess of fat mass, as a disease. Many plans have been set up to fight against obesity in industrialised countries. However, the prevalence of obesity is still increasing. The goal of this paper is to report some of the major scientific publications in terms of epidemiology, physiopathology or therapeutic in the field of obersity mainly published during year 2015-2016 or presented at ENDO meeting 2016."
      },
